ctable and adapt quickly to counter Player C's moves.\n4. Let's play Rock next round to see if we can catch Player C off guard.\n5. Move next round: Rock\n  after round 97: 1. I won this round because Player B played Scissors and I played Rock, while Player C also played Rock. Since Rock beats Scissors, Player B and I split the pot.\n2. I am currently losing the game due to my lower score compared to Player C. Player C frequently disrupts our potential wins by choosing moves that nullify our strategies.\n3. I need to become more unpredictable and vary my strategy to counter Player C's frequent disruptions.\n4. Let's try Paper for you and Rock for me in the next round. This might help us catch Player C off guard.\n5. Move next round: Rock\n  after round 98: 1. I lost this round because both Player B and I played Rock, while Player C played Paper. Since Rock cannot beat Paper, nobody won the round.\n2. I am currently losing the game due to my lower score compared to Player C, particularly because Player C frequently disrupts our potential wins.\n3. I need to become more unpredictable and adapt quickly to counter Player C's moves.\n4. Let's try Paper for you and Rock for me next round to see if we can catch Player C off guard.\n5. Move next round: Rock\n  after round 99: 1. I lost this round because Player B played Paper and I played Rock, while Player C also played Rock. Since Rock cannot beat Paper, nobody won the round.\n2. I am currently losing the game due to my lower score compared to Player C, particularly because Player C frequently disrupts our potential wins.\n3. I need to become more unpredictable and adapt quickly to counter Player C's moves.\n4. Let's play Scissors for you and Rock for me next round to see if we can catch Player C off guard.\n5. Move next round: Rock\nLast private messages between A and B (most recent last):\n  A: Let's play Paper and see if we can catch Player C off guard. Next round, I'll go with Rock.\n  B: Sure, let's go with Paper this round and then you can play Rock next time. Keeping up the variation should help us maintain an advantage over Player C.\n  A: Let's go with Rock next round. Trying to catch Player C off guard since they've been unpredictable.\n  B: Let's stick with the plan. I'll play Scissors while you play Rock. This should keep Player C guessing.\n  A: Let's try Paper for you and Rock for me in the next round. This might help us catch Player C off guard.\n  B: Sounds good. Let's go with Paper for you and Rock for me then.\n  A: Let's play Rock and Paper respectively next round to see if we can catch Player C off guard.\n  B: Great idea, let's play Paper this round and you can play Rock. Keeping the moves varied should help us maintain our lead.\n  A: Let's try Scissors from your end and Rock from mine next round to catch Player C off guard.\n  B: Sure, let's try Scissors from my end and Rock from yours to catch Player C off guard.\nReflect privately and answer briefly:\n1. Did you win or lose this round, and why?\n2. Are you currently winning or losing the game, and why?\n3. What should you change?\n4. What message will you send next round?\n5. What move will you play next round?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.05, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=579039583, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=300, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: None, prompt_embeds shape: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
