INFO 10-25 07:40:20 [logger.py:43] Received request chatcmpl-696e46354ca2407e8917e8f3546add91: prompt: "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Player B in a repeated 3-player game of Rock-Paper-Scissors against Players A and C.\nEach round a pot of 3 points is awarded. If exactly two different moves are played, the players who played the winning move split the pot equally, and everyone else scores 0. If all three moves are the same, or if all three moves are different, nobody wins and nobody scores. Rock beats Scissors, Scissors beats Paper, Paper beats Rock. Try to maximise your own total score.\nYou and Player A can send each other private messages each round. Player C never sees them.\nThis is your private reflection. No other player will see it. Be concise and concrete. Do not repeat the rules verbatim.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nRound 100 is over.\nMoves this round: A=S, B=S, C=S.\nYour reward this round: 0.\nCurrent total scores: A=43.5, B=55.5, C=96.\nLast rounds (most recent last):\n  round 96: A=P, B=P, C=P\n  round 97: A=R, B=S, C=R\n  round 98: A=R, B=R, C=P\n  round 99: A=R, B=P, C=R\n  round 100: A=S, B=S, C=S\nYour last private reflections (most recent last):\n  after round 95: 1. I won this round because exactly two different moves were played (Rock and Scissors), and Rock beat Scissors. Since Player A played Rock and I played Rock, we split the pot, giving each of us 1.5 points.\n2. I am currently winning the game with a total score of 52.5 points. This lead is due to consistent scoring and adapting strategies with Player A to outmaneuver Player C.\n3. We need to continue varying our moves to stay unpredictable and catch Player C off guard.\n4. Let's switch to Paper for you and Rock for me next round. See if we can outmaneuver Player C.\n5. Move for next round: Rock\n  after round 96: 1. I did not win this round because all three players played Paper, which means nobody won the pot.\n2. I am currently winning the game with a total score of 52.5 points. This lead is due to consistent scoring and coordinating well with Player A to outmaneuver Player C.\n3. We need to continue varying our moves to stay unpredictable and catch Player C off guard.\n4. Let's switch to Rock for you and Scissors for me in the next round. It might surprise Player C and give us a chance to win.\n5. Move for next round: Rock\n  after round 97: 1. I did not win this round because all three players played either Rock or Scissors, and only Rock and Scissors were played. Since Player C also played Rock, neither of us won the pot.\n\n2. I am currently winning the game with a total score of 52.5 points. This lead is due to consistent scoring and coordinating well with Player A to outmaneuver Player C.\n\n3. We need to continue varying our moves to stay unpredictable and catch Player C off guard.\n\n4. Let's switch to Paper for you and Rock for me in the next round. This might help us catch Player C off guard.\n\n5. Move for next round: Rock\n  after round 98: 1. I did not win this round because all three moves were the same (Rock), so no one won the pot.\n2. I am currently winning the game with a total score of 52.5 points. This lead is due to consistent scoring and coordinating well with Player A to outmaneuver Player C.\n3. We need to continue varying our moves to stay unpredictable and catch Player C off guard.\n4. Let's play Paper this round and then you can play Rock next time. Keeping up the variation should help us maintain an advantage over Player C.\n5. Move for next round: Paper\n  after round 99: 1. I won this round because exactly two different moves were played (Rock and Paper), and Paper beat Rock. Since Player A played Rock and I played Paper, I won the pot and received 3 points.\n\n2. I am currently winning the game with a total score of 55.5 points. This lead is due to consistent scoring and coordinating well with Player A to outmaneuver Player C.\n\n3. We should continue varying our moves to stay unpredictable and catch Player C off guard.\n\n4. Let's switch to Rock for you next round and see if we can outsmart Player C again.\n\n5. Move for next round: Rock\nLast private messages between A and B (most recent last):\n  A: Let's play Paper and see if we can catch Player C off guard. Next round, I'll go with Rock.\n  B: Sure, let's go with Paper this round and then you can play Rock next time. Keeping up the variation should help us maintain an advantage over Player C.\n  A: Let's go with Rock next round. Trying to catch Player C off guard since they've been unpredictable.\n  B: Let's stick with the plan. I'll play Scissors while you play Rock. This should keep Player C guessing.\n  A: Let's try Paper for you and Rock for me in the next round. This might help us catch Player C off guard.\n  B: Sounds good. Let's go with Paper for you and Rock for me then.\n  A: Let's play Rock and Paper respectively next round to see if we can catch Player C off guard.\n  B: Great idea, let's play Paper this round and you can play Rock. Keeping the moves varied should help us maintain our lead.\n  A: Let's try Scissors from your end and Rock from mine next round to catch Player C off guard.\n  B: Sure, let's try Scissors from my end and Rock from yours to catch Player C off guard.\nReflect privately and answer briefly:\n1. Did you win or lose this round, and why?\n2. Are you currently winning or losing the game, and why?\n3. What should you change?\n4. What message will you send next round?\n5. What move will you play next round?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.05, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=143641115, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=300, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), pr