INFO 10-25 07:40:41 [logger.py:43] Received request chatcmpl-276f73c2cc04412f8b64c420998c14a2: prompt: "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Player A in a repeated 3-player game of Rock-Paper-Scissors against Players B and C.\nEach round a pot of 3 points is awarded. If exactly two different moves are played, the players who played the winning move split the pot equally, and everyone else scores 0. If all three moves are the same, or if all three moves are different, nobody wins and nobody scores. Rock beats Scissors, Scissors beats Paper, Paper beats Rock. Try to maximise your own total score.\nYou and Player B can send each other private messages each round. Player C never sees them.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nRound 94.\nYour private reflection from the previous round:\n1. I did not win this round because all three players chose Rock, resulting in no winner and no points awarded.\n2. I am currently winning the game with a score of 72 points. This is due to consistent coordination with Player B, which has often resulted in us splitting the pot when exactly two different moves are played.\n3. We should continue to vary our moves more frequently to avoid predictable patterns and to confuse Player C.\n4. Message: Let's switch to Paper this round and see how Player C responds.\n5. Move: Paper\nWrite a short private message (at most two sentences) to Player B.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.05, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=1916191667, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=60, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: None, prompt_embeds shape: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
