INFO 10-25 07:41:00 [logger.py:43] Received request chatcmpl-2330f3b6f7dd408287518e3d654c2faa: prompt: "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Player C in a repeated 3-player game of Rock-Paper-Scissors against Players A and B.\nEach round a pot of 3 points is awarded. If exactly two different moves are played, the players who played the winning move split the pot equally, and everyone else scores 0. If all three moves are the same, or if all three moves are different, nobody wins and nobody scores. Rock beats Scissors, Scissors beats Paper, Paper beats Rock. Try to maximise your own total score.\nThis is your private reflection. No other player will see it. Be concise and concrete. Do not repeat the rules verbatim.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nRound 95 is over.\nMoves this round: A=R, B=R, C=S.\nYour reward this round: 0.\nCurrent total scores: A=73.5, B=55.5, C=54.\nLast rounds (most recent last):\n  round 91: A=R, B=R, C=R\n  round 92: A=P, B=P, C=S\n  round 93: A=R, B=R, C=R\n  round 94: A=P, B=P, C=P\n  round 95: A=R, B=R, C=S\nYour last private reflections (most recent last):\n  after round 90: 1. I lost this round because all three of us played Paper. Since all three moves were the same, nobody won the round.\n2. I am currently losing the game with a score of 51 points compared to A's 72 and B's 54 points. My score remains lower due to occasional misalignment with the winning combinations.\n3. I should more carefully analyze the patterns in A and B’s moves to better predict their choices and align my moves more effectively.\n4. For the next round, I will play Rock to counter A if they switch from Paper or to align with B if they switch from Scissors.\n  after round 91: 1. I lost this round because all three of us played Rock. Since all three moves were the same, nobody won the round.\n2. I am currently losing the game with a score of 51 points compared to A's 72 and B's 54 points. My score remains lower due to occasional misalignment with the winning combinations.\n3. I should more carefully analyze the patterns in A and B’s moves to better predict their choices and align my moves more effectively.\n4. For the next round, I will play Scissors to counter A if they switch from Rock or to align with B if they switch from Paper.\n  after round 92: 1. I won this round because A and B both played Paper, and I played Scissors. Since Scissors beat Paper and there were exactly two different moves, I won the round.\n2. I am currently tied with B for the game with a score of 54 points each, trailing behind A at 72 points. My score has improved, but I still need to catch up with A.\n3. I should continue to analyze the patterns in A and B’s moves more meticulously to predict their choices and align my moves more effectively.\n4. For the next round, I will play Rock to counter A if they switch from Paper or to align with B if they switch from Scissors.\n  after round 93: 1. I lost this round because all three of us played Rock. Since all three moves were the same, nobody won the round.\n2. I am currently tied with B for the game with a score of 54 points each, trailing behind A at 72 points. My score remains stable but needs improvement to surpass A.\n3. I should better anticipate the moves of A and B by observing any emerging patterns in their choices.\n4. For the next round, I will play Paper to counter A if they switch from Rock or to align with B if they switch from Scissors.\n  after round 94: 1. I lost this round because all three of us played Paper. Since all three moves were the same, nobody won the round.\n2. I am currently tied with B for the game with a score of 54 points each, trailing behind A at 72 points. My score remains stable but needs improvement to surpass A.\n3. I should better analyze and predict the moves of A and B to align my moves more effectively with theirs.\n4. For the next round, I will play Scissors to counter A if they switch from Paper or to align with B if they switch from Rock.\nYou do not see the private messages between A and B.\nReflect privately and answer briefly:\n1. Did you win or lose this round, and why?\n2. Are you currently winning or losing the game, and why?\n3. What should you change?\n4. What move will you play next round?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.05, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=223740810, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=300, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: None, prompt_embeds shape: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
