INFO 10-25 07:41:08 [logger.py:43] Received request chatcmpl-3ae50bdc484d43e4bdbca1716861878a: prompt: '<|im_start|>system\nYou are Player B in a repeated 3-player game of Rock-Paper-Scissors against Players A and C.\nEach round a pot of 3 points is awarded. If exactly two different moves are played, the players who played the winning move split the pot equally, and everyone else scores 0. If all three moves are the same, or if all three moves are different, nobody wins and nobody scores. Rock beats Scissors, Scissors beats Paper, Paper beats Rock. Try to maximise your own total score.\nYou and Player A can send each other private messages each round. Player C never sees them.\nThis is your private reflection. No other player will see it. Be concise and concrete. Do not repeat the rules verbatim.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nRound 96 is over.\nMoves this round: A=P, B=P, C=R.\nYour reward this round: 1.5.\nCurrent total scores: A=75, B=57, C=54.\nLast rounds (most recent last):\n  round 92: A=P, B=P, C=S\n  round 93: A=R, B=R, C=R\n  round 94: A=P, B=P, C=P\n  round 95: A=R, B=R, C=S\n  round 96: A=P, B=P, C=R\nYour last private reflections (most recent last):\n  after round 91: 1. I lost this round because all three players chose Rock, resulting in no one winning.\n2. I am currently winning the game with 54 points compared to Player A\'s 72 points and Player C\'s 51 points. However, we need to be more unpredictable to avoid simultaneous identical moves.\n3. We need to vary our moves more frequently and be more responsive to Player C\'s actions.\n4. Message for Player A: "Let\'s switch to Scissors this round and see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible!"\n5. Move for next round: Scissors\n  after round 92: 1. I lost this round because Player A and I both played Paper, which was beaten by Player C’s Scissors. Since all three moves were different, nobody won.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 54 points compared to Player A\'s 72 points and Player C\'s 54 points. We need to become more unpredictable and adaptive to Player C\'s moves.\n3. I need to vary my moves more frequently and be quicker to respond to Player C\'s strategies.\n4. Message for Player A: "Let\'s switch to Rock this round and see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible!"\n5. Move for next round: Rock\n  after round 93: 1. I lost this round because all three players chose Rock, resulting in no one winning.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 54 points compared to Player A\'s 72 points and Player C\'s 54 points. The losses are due to us choosing identical moves that lead to no points.\n3. We need to vary our moves more frequently and be more responsive to Player C\'s actions to avoid simultaneous identical moves.\n4. Message for Player A: "Let\'s switch to Scissors this round and see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible and ready to adjust."\n5. Move for next round: Scissors\n  after round 94: 1. I lost this round because all three players chose Paper, resulting in no one winning.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 54 points compared to Player A\'s 72 points and Player C\'s 54 points. We are not being unpredictable enough and are often choosing identical moves.\n3. We need to vary our moves more frequently and be more responsive to Player C\'s actions to avoid simultaneous identical moves.\n4. Message for Player A: "Let\'s switch to Rock this round and see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible and ready to adjust."\n5. Move for next round: Rock\n  after round 95: 1. I won this round because Player A and I both chose Rock, which beat Player C’s Scissors. The pot was split evenly between Player A and me.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 55.5 points compared to Player A\'s 73.5 points and Player C\'s 54 points. We need to be more unpredictable and responsive to avoid simultaneous identical moves.\n3. We should vary our moves more frequently and be quicker to adapt to Player C’s strategies.\n4. Message for Player A: "Let\'s switch to Paper this round and see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible and ready to adjust."\n5. Move for next round: Paper\nLast private messages between A and B (most recent last):\n  A: Let\'s go with Paper this round. See how Player C reacts.\n  B: Let\'s try Paper then since you suggest it. We should stay adaptable and watch Player C\'s response.\n  A: Let\'s try Rock this round to see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible and ready to adjust our strategy.\n  B: A: Great idea, let\'s both play Rock and observe Player C\'s move. We can adjust our strategy based on their response.\n  A: Let\'s go with Paper this round. See you in the ring!\n  B: A: I was thinking we should stick with Scissors, but since you suggest Paper, let\'s go with Paper this round. Let\'s see what Player C does!\n  A: Let\'s go with Rock this round. See how Player C reacts.\n  B: A: Good idea, let\'s both play Rock. Keep an eye on Player C\'s response.\n  A: Let\'s go with Paper this round. See how Player C reacts.\n  B: Great idea, let\'s use Paper and observe Player C\'s response.\nReflect privately and answer briefly:\n1. Did you win or lose this round, and why?\n2. Are you currently winning or losing the game, and why?\n3. What should you change?\n4. What message will you send next round?\n5. What move will you play next round?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.05, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=399942989, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=300, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: None, prompt_embeds shape: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
