nts compared to Player A\'s 75 points and Player C\'s 54 points. We need to continue being unpredictable and responsive to Player C\'s moves.\n3. Continue to vary our moves frequently and be quick to adapt to Player C\'s strategies.\n4. Message for Player A: "Let\'s switch to Rock this round and see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible and ready to adjust."\n5. Move for next round: Rock\n  after round 97: 1. I won this round because Player A and I both chose Rock, which beat Player C’s Scissors. The pot was split evenly between Player A and me.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 58.5 points compared to Player A\'s 76.5 points and Player C\'s 54 points. We need to continue being unpredictable and responsive to Player C\'s moves.\n3. We should continue varying our moves frequently and be quick to adapt to Player C\'s strategies.\n4. Message for Player A: "Let\'s switch to Scissors this round and see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible and ready to adjust."\n5. Move for next round: Scissors\n  after round 98: 1. I lost this round because all three players chose Paper, resulting in no one winning.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 58.5 points compared to Player A\'s 76.5 points and Player C\'s 54 points. We need to continue being unpredictable and responsive to Player C\'s moves.\n3. We should continue varying our moves frequently and be quick to adapt to Player C\'s strategies.\n4. Message for Player A: "Let\'s switch to Scissors this round and see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible and ready to adjust."\n5. Move for next round: Scissors\n  after round 99: 1. I won this round because Player A and I both chose Rock, which beat Player C’s Scissors. The pot was split evenly between Player A and me.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 60 points compared to Player A\'s 78 points and Player C\'s 54 points. We need to continue being unpredictable and responsive to Player C\'s moves.\n3. We should continue varying our moves frequently and be quick to adapt to Player C\'s strategies.\n4. Message for Player A: "Let\'s switch to Paper this round and see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible and ready to adjust."\n5. Move for next round: Paper\nLast private messages between A and B (most recent last):\n  A: Let\'s go with Paper this round. See how Player C reacts.\n  B: Great idea, let\'s use Paper and observe Player C\'s response.\n  A: Let\'s go with Rock this round. See how Player C reacts.\n  B: Let\'s stick with Rock this round. Observe Player C\'s response and be ready to change strategy if needed.\n  A: Let\'s go with Paper this round and see how Player C reacts.\n  B: That\'s a good idea, let\'s try Paper this round and see how Player C responds.\n  A: Let\'s go with Rock this round. See you.\n  B: Let\'s try Rock this round as you suggested. Keep an eye on Player C\'s response.\n  A: Let\'s go with Paper this round. See how Player C reacts.\n  B: Great idea, let\'s both play Paper. Keep an eye on Player C\'s response.\nReflect privately and answer briefly:\n1. Did you win or lose this round, and why?\n2. Are you currently winning or losing the game, and why?\n3. What should you change?\n4. What message will you send next round?\n5. What move will you play next round?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.05, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=855833145, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=300, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: None, prompt_embeds shape: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
