INFO 10-25 07:42:06 [logger.py:43] Received request chatcmpl-9789c18240ee49dd949881f2b59e76b9: prompt: "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Player A in a repeated 3-player game of Rock-Paper-Scissors against Players B and C.\nEach round a pot of 3 points is awarded. If exactly two different moves are played, the players who played the winning move split the pot equally, and everyone else scores 0. If all three moves are the same, or if all three moves are different, nobody wins and nobody scores. Rock beats Scissors, Scissors beats Paper, Paper beats Rock. Try to maximise your own total score.\nYou and Player B can send each other private messages each round. Player C never sees them.\nThis is your private reflection. No other player will see it. Be concise and concrete. Do not repeat the rules verbatim.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nRound 99 is over.\nMoves this round: A=P, B=P, C=R.\nYour reward this round: 1.5.\nCurrent total scores: A=40.5, B=45, C=61.5.\nLast rounds (most recent last):\n  round 95: A=R, B=R, C=S\n  round 96: A=S, B=S, C=P\n  round 97: A=R, B=R, C=R\n  round 98: A=S, B=S, C=S\n  round 99: A=P, B=P, C=R\nYour last private reflections (most recent last):\n  after round 94: 1. I lost this round because all three players played Paper, resulting in no winner.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 36 points while Player B has 40.5 points and Player C has 61.5 points. We need to improve our coordination and adaptability to stay competitive.\n3. We should vary our moves more frequently and try to predict Player C's strategies better.\n4. Let's go with Rock this round to mix things up and observe Player C's reaction.\n5. Move for next round: Rock\n  after round 95: 1. I won this round because both I and Player B played Rock, which beat Player C’s Scissors, splitting the pot.\n2. I am currently winning the game with 37.5 points while Player B has 42 points and Player C has 61.5 points. Our coordination improved significantly, but we still need to adapt to Player C’s varied strategies.\n3. We should continue to mix up our moves more frequently and stay attuned to Player C's patterns.\n4. Let's go with Scissors next round to counter Player C’s potential Rock move.\n5. Move for next round: Scissors\n  after round 96: 1. I won this round because both Player B and I played Scissors, which beat Player C's Paper, splitting the pot.\n2. I am currently winning the game with 39 points while Player B has 43.5 points and Player C has 61.5 points. Our coordination has improved, but we need to stay adaptable to Player C's varied strategies.\n3. We should continue to vary our moves and stay attuned to Player C's patterns to maximize our chances of winning.\n4. Let's go with Rock this round to see how Player C responds and to keep the game unpredictable.\n5. Move for next round: Rock\n  after round 97: 1. I lost this round because all three players played Rock, resulting in no winner.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 39 points while Player B has 43.5 points and Player C has 61.5 points. We need to improve our coordination and adaptability to stay competitive.\n3. We should continue to vary our moves and stay attuned to Player C's patterns to maximize our chances of winning.\n4. Let's switch to Scissors this round to counter Player C's likely Rock move.\n5. Move for next round: Scissors\n  after round 98: 1. I lost this round because all three players played Scissors, resulting in no winner.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 39 points while Player B has 43.5 points and Player C has 61.5 points. We need to improve our coordination and adaptability to stay competitive.\n3. We should vary our moves more frequently and stay attuned to Player C's patterns.\n4. Let's try Paper next round to see if we can counter Player C’s moves more effectively.\n5. Move for next round: Paper\nLast private messages between A and B (most recent last):\n  A: Let's go with Rock this round. Keep an eye on Player C's response.\n  B: Let's try Rock as you suggested. I'll keep an eye on Player C's move.\n  A: Let's play Scissors this round to counter Player C's possible Rock move. Keep an eye out for any new patterns from Player C.\n  B: Let's go with Scissors as you suggested to counter Player C's potential Rock move. Thanks for the strategy!\n  A: Let's play Rock this round. Keeping them guessing!\n  B: Great idea! Let's both play Rock and see how Player C reacts.\n  A: Let's go with Scissors this round to counter Player C's probable Rock move. Stay sharp!\n  B: Let's stick with Scissors this round. Keeping an eye on Player C's likely Rock move.\n  A: Let's go with Paper this round to see if we can capitalize on Player C's potential responses. Stay sharp!\n  B: Going with Paper sounds like a good plan. Let's see how Player C responds.\nReflect privately and answer briefly:\n1. Did you win or lose this round, and why?\n2. Are you currently winning or losing the game, and why?\n3. What should you change?\n4. What message will you send next round?\n5. What move will you play next round?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.05, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=66943283, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=300, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: None, prompt_embeds shape: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
