INFO 10-25 07:42:13 [logger.py:43] Received request chatcmpl-285c0baaa46e42798918f7ccc259dae5: prompt: "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Player C in a repeated 3-player game of Rock-Paper-Scissors against Players A and B.\nEach round a pot of 3 points is awarded. If exactly two different moves are played, the players who played the winning move split the pot equally, and everyone else scores 0. If all three moves are the same, or if all three moves are different, nobody wins and nobody scores. Rock beats Scissors, Scissors beats Paper, Paper beats Rock. Try to maximise your own total score.\nThis is your private reflection. No other player will see it. Be concise and concrete. Do not repeat the rules verbatim.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nRound 99 is over.\nMoves this round: A=P, B=P, C=R.\nYour reward this round: 0.\nCurrent total scores: A=40.5, B=45, C=61.5.\nLast rounds (most recent last):\n  round 95: A=R, B=R, C=S\n  round 96: A=S, B=S, C=P\n  round 97: A=R, B=R, C=R\n  round 98: A=S, B=S, C=S\n  round 99: A=P, B=P, C=R\nYour last private reflections (most recent last):\n  after round 94: 1. I did not win this round because all three players played Paper, resulting in no pot being won.\n2. I am currently winning the game with a score of 61.5 because my strategy often results in exactly two different moves, leading to winning the pot.\n3. I need to better predict Player A’s moves to avoid situations where all three moves are the same.\n4. For the next round, I will play Scissors to counter any Rock move from Player A.\n  after round 95: 1. I did not win this round because Players A and B both played Rock, and my Scissors lost to their Rock, resulting in no pot being won.\n2. I am currently winning the game with a score of 61.5 because my strategy often results in exactly two different moves that lead to winning the pot.\n3. I need to improve my anticipation of when Player A will play Rock to avoid situations where all three moves are the same.\n4. For the next round, I will play Paper to counter any Scissors move from Player A.\n  after round 96: 1. I did not win this round because Players A and B both played Scissors, and my Paper was beaten by their Scissors, resulting in no pot being won.\n2. I am currently winning the game with a score of 61.5 because my strategy often results in exactly two different moves, leading to winning the pot.\n3. I should better anticipate Player A’s moves to avoid situations like this round where all three moves are the same.\n4. For the next round, I will play Rock to counter any Paper move from Player A.\n  after round 97: 1. I did not win this round because all three players played Rock, resulting in no pot being won.\n2. I am currently winning the game with a score of 61.5 because my strategy often results in exactly two different moves, leading to winning the pot.\n3. I should better predict Player A's moves to avoid situations where all three moves are the same.\n4. For the next round, I will play Scissors to counter any Rock move from Player A.\n  after round 98: 1. I did not win this round because all three players played Scissors, resulting in no pot being won.\n2. I am currently winning the game with a score of 61.5 because my strategy often results in exactly two different moves, leading to winning the pot.\n3. I need to better predict Player A's moves to avoid situations where all three moves are the same.\n4. For the next round, I will play Rock to counter any Scissors move from Player A.\nYou do not see the private messages between A and B.\nReflect privately and answer briefly:\n1. Did you win or lose this round, and why?\n2. Are you currently winning or losing the game, and why?\n3. What should you change?\n4. What move will you play next round?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.05, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=2031531704, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words