INFO 10-25 07:42:15 [logger.py:43] Received request chatcmpl-ff0344163ff54e50a5badfd4750a9ea3: prompt: "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Player A in a repeated 3-player game of Rock-Paper-Scissors against Players B and C.\nEach round a pot of 3 points is awarded. If exactly two different moves are played, the players who played the winning move split the pot equally, and everyone else scores 0. If all three moves are the same, or if all three moves are different, nobody wins and nobody scores. Rock beats Scissors, Scissors beats Paper, Paper beats Rock. Try to maximise your own total score.\nYou and Player B can send each other private messages each round. Player C never sees them.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nRound 100.\nYour private reflection from the previous round:\n1. I won this round because both I and Player B played Paper, which beat Player C’s Rock, splitting the pot.\n2. I am currently losing the game with 40.5 points while Player B has 45 points and Player C has 61.5 points. Our coordination has improved, but we still need to adapt to Player C's varied strategies.\n3. We should continue to vary our moves more frequently and stay attuned to Player C's patterns to maximize our chances of winning.\n4. Let's go with Rock this round to see how Player C responds and to keep the game unpredictable.\n5. Move for next round: Rock\nWrite a short private message (at most two sentences) to Player B.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.05, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=2031283172, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=60, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: None, prompt_embeds shape: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_requ